<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Historia Tolteca-Chichimeca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Historia Tolteca-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chichimeca">Chichimeca</a> is a 16th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahuatl">Nahuatl</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> from Cuauhtinchan in Puebla, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, combining text with pictorial maps. Written around 1545–1565, it records the migrations of the Tolteca-Chichimeca from Tollan to Cholula, their seizure of the city in the 12th century, and the history and land claims of the people of Cuauhtinchan. It is now held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bibliotheque-nationale-de-france">National Library of France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/historia-tolteca-chichimeca.jpg" alt="Historia Tolteca-Chichimeca" width="320" height="367" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ToltecaChichimeca_Chicomostoc.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
